1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,200
We used Codex inside a process deliberately designed to keep judgment human.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:13,300
The Flywheel routes an approved spec through dependency-aware beads, bounded execution, evidence, and durable handoffs.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:22,300
Only the next ready bead moves. Its worker gets file scope, invariants, and verification before it edits anything.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:31,200
Then we run the real CLI underneath the demo. The trace stays readable: source snapshot, replay, and offline proof.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,200
Tests and review scale with the risk. No gate is only decorative.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,300
The evidence persists. Humans decide when the work is done.
